{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_02bc5fbfa7cb44aebd774540a3a09d3cfc0c43b5c3c0c0e83116eddb303ccf35"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Licensing is PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0: free for non-commercial use while businesses require a license, with fees distributed among contributors at project leads' discretion."},{"claim_ids":["clm_229e6ca4f6bf0ead48ea971b912c24650e8dc180037be8af1d379ddbe3a366b4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"move-file updates import references across the codebase, and find-usages locates symbol usages across files."},{"claim_ids":["clm_49a7ab7047c752bac63c825d7803ef6bc010854518a7bcfce9b6b84016f99058"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The design goal is surgical edits: instead of regenerating whole files, operations change only the targeted code and its references, saving tokens and preserving agent cognitive capacity."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6b671edf2be68ad3614e9601412c80870975d15e5bf08ce19fe5ea092aa9cb0f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the repo is optimized for Claude Code; contributors are told to have Claude set up pre/post commit hooks, pick a 'good first issue', assign it to themselves, and can direct work by issue number."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7598f12684d23327c3b60a57022f96186e6869909dad63ff3c4a7d9604ebc57e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool uses ts-morph for AST manipulation and @phenomnomnominal/tsquery for node selection, and is built with TypeScript."},{"claim_ids":["clm_77150e6643c5ad48dfd7f28de9c8253a05afb12c10d43af4fd51fc5b3b6769d5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The package is installed globally via npm as 'refakts'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8068648ab0810c879b3438f28542e2ecdcefa7424968b2168637ddbc8365af05"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: tests are fixture-based under tests/fixtures with .input.ts, .expected.ts, and .expected.txt files per command, and npm run test:coverage checks for uncovered use cases."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8ec2b73f4db1b63018039ccf43c79e1df2d8294dcd9f5eb2c73d82d04aecfe19"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The select command supports regex, range, structural, and boundary modes, e.g. --range with start/end regexes and --boundaries \"function\"."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ca1c355f024b7f3e90d3806a36c822765b5dbf32cb8c117af4b2ab0957c274ed"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"RefakTS is a command-line tool exposing commands including extract-variable, inline-variable, rename, select, sort-methods, find-usages, and move-file."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d9e58cfff72b4e4ead069fbc96b63d0d73132f2665c3c68a931efe744cc64bd4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: post-commit hooks scan for quality issues (oversized functions, unused methods, comments, duplication, large changes) and automatically prompt the AI agent with corrective guidance."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e4ddb0d3756605404e91b2eb8237ffdaf35b0076762831a19d275b1d807f8609"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project targets AI agents making multi-location code changes (renames, extractions) and is positioned as built by AI agents for AI agents, with a roadmap managed by Claude instances."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ed1f2771b29ebfa83dc3074d4d40dd5e0040e9839bfeabd2d3bea266bbdb2ca0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is explicitly labeled a proof of concept demonstrating the core concept with basic refactoring operations, with more commands in development."}],"claim_ids":["clm_02bc5fbfa7cb44aebd774540a3a09d3cfc0c43b5c3c0c0e83116eddb303ccf35","clm_229e6ca4f6bf0ead48ea971b912c24650e8dc180037be8af1d379ddbe3a366b4","clm_49a7ab7047c752bac63c825d7803ef6bc010854518a7bcfce9b6b84016f99058","clm_6b671edf2be68ad3614e9601412c80870975d15e5bf08ce19fe5ea092aa9cb0f","clm_7598f12684d23327c3b60a57022f96186e6869909dad63ff3c4a7d9604ebc57e","clm_77150e6643c5ad48dfd7f28de9c8253a05afb12c10d43af4fd51fc5b3b6769d5","clm_8068648ab0810c879b3438f28542e2ecdcefa7424968b2168637ddbc8365af05","clm_8ec2b73f4db1b63018039ccf43c79e1df2d8294dcd9f5eb2c73d82d04aecfe1